{
  "_comment": "Common allowlist baseline — synced to all machines via deploy.sh. Edit here, commit, then run deploy.sh on each device. Two rules of thumb: (1) only bounded commands belong in allowedTools — a rule like 'Bash(rm *)' or 'Bash(zsh -i -c *)' makes every other entry decorative; (2) deniedTools is evaluated before allowedTools and is the only part that can stop something. This file is a convenience baseline, not a security boundary: it is per-user config, and the agent can still propose a command you have not pre-approved. See shared/allowlist-common.md.",
